  "details": "Often, worlds are created collaboratively by teams. For example, the now Emmy-winning Uncanny Alley was a collaboration between The Ferryman Collective, MetaRick and Screaming Color.\n\nHowever, if you look at the world page, only MetaRick is officially listed as the creator. This means that if I were searching for work by Screaming Color, Uncanny Alley wouldn’t appear.\n\nCredits are important in this community, both for recognising people’s contributions and for discovering their work. I’d suggest adding a secondary credits section to World pages, where everyone who contributed can be properly attributed and linked to their profile.\n\nThink of it a little like IMDb for VRChat worlds: a world has a primary creator, but also a full set of searchable credits showing everyone who helped make it.",
